## Expired lease refuses renewal on the production maintenance path (red -> green, real PostgreSQL)

test=apps/dispatcher/test/integration/leases.integration.test.ts
      "does not renew an expired lease on an active task and requires a stop proof"
      "adopts an expired lease only when the runtime confirms the same generation running"
command:
  TEST_DATABASE_ADMIN_URL=postgres://moyu@127.0.0.1:55432/postgres \
    corepack pnpm --filter @moyu/dispatcher exec vitest run \
    test/integration/leases.integration.test.ts --reporter=verbose

This calls `maintainLeases` (the 5-second production loop at dispatcher.ts:121), not an
unused helper. The fixture has an active lease bound to a task in `running` and moves
`expires_at` into the past.

red before the operations.ts guard:
  × does not renew an expired lease on an active task and requires a stop proof
    AssertionError: expected '2026-11-07T16:29:47.503Z' to be '2026-11-07T15:29:46.500Z'
    (the maintenance heartbeat extended the expired lease by an hour)
  Tests 1 failed | 5 skipped (6)

green after the guard:
  ✓ does not renew an expired lease on an active task and requires a stop proof 25ms
  ✓ adopts an expired lease only when the runtime confirms the same generation running 15ms
  Tests 2 passed | 4 skipped (6)

The first test asserts `expires_at` is unchanged, state stays `active`, and the lease is
`recovery_state='blocked'` waiting for `execution_stop_proof` after an idle snapshot. The
second pins the intentional exemption: when the Bridge authoritatively reports the same
generation `running`, `reconcileLeases` adopts it, extends expiry and records an `adopted`
event; an expired generation with no such confirmation is never revived.

Code scope:
- operations.ts `maintainLeases`: both renewal statements now require
  `(expires_at is null or expires_at > now())`; expired generations fall through to
  reconcileLeases.
- leases.ts `acquireOn`: expiration is read as `(expires_at <= now())` in the same locking
  statement, so the lock check uses the database clock that writes expiry, not `Date.now()`.
- leases.ts `reconcileLeases`: the `running` adopt branch is documented as the intentional
  continuation exemption; all other/unknown states stay fenced.
- `renewExecutionLease` was deleted: it had no production call site.

## Verdict

Both stores were restarted (bridge 2107062 -> 2114387, dispatcher 2112165 -> 2114545);
ticket/assignment/admission/base/model/worktree and PG task/delivery/lease link are identical
field by field, the sync cursor advanced 100 -> 102 on post-restart traffic, and an expired
lease cannot be renewed or re-acquired without a stop proof. Item 4 accepted.
